 ## Overview
-Alpha invariance is the property that volume rendering results (specifically the alpha compositing weights) remain invariant under arbitrary scene scaling, requiring volume density $\sigma$ to scale inversely with the ray segment length $d$ [S1]. It solves the problem of optimization failure in neural radiance fields when scene scales change, where standard parameterizations either fail to produce sufficient density for small intervals or cause cloudiness for large intervals [S1]. It sets itself apart from sibling methods by providing a theoretical foundation for density initialization and activation function selection, rather than just a heuristic initialization step.
