 ## Background
-The concept originates from the analysis of neural radiance fields (NeRF) and their sensitivity to scene scale [S1]. It was identified as a critical factor in preventing optimization failure due to floaters or cloudiness when scenes are scaled [S1]. The term "Alpha Invariance" was coined to describe the desired property of $\alpha$ invariance with respect to scene scaling [S1]. The related term "Inverse Scaling Analysis" refers to the empirical method of analyzing how $\sigma$ changes with $k$ [S1].
